      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-142458",
      ":question/problem": "The table below gives the values of $x$ that satisfy $P(X \\ge x) = p$, where $X$ has a student's $t$-distribution $T_{k}$ with $k$ degrees of freedom. Given that the random variable $X\u223cT_{15}$, find the value of $x$ such that $P(X \\le x) = 0.95$.\n\n| $k\u2216p$ | $0.100$ | $0.050$ | $0.025$ | $0.010$ | $0.005$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $15$ | $1.341$ | $1.753$ | $2.131$ | $2.602$ | $2.947$ |\n| $16$ | $1.337$ | $1.746$ | $2.120$ | $2.583$ | $2.921$ |\n| $17$ | $1.333$ | $1.740$ | $2.110$ | $2.576$ | $2.898$ |"
